WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.980
- In "Halloween: The
Curse of Michael Myers,"

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.540
a new nuclear family lives
in the old Myers' house.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.810
Well, you know, it isn't
exactly the Myers' house,

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.340
but it's closer than the monstrosity

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.740
they used in "Halloween 5."

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.730
The parents are named
John and Debra Strode,

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.190
the aunt and uncle of Laurie
Strode from "Halloween I,"

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.470
who are named after the
producers of that original movie:

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.120
John Carpenter and Debra Hill.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.550
For added authenticity,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.010
John Strode's first line in the movie

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.840
sounds exactly like
something John Carpenter

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.240
would have said after
making "Halloween II."

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.183
- Enough of this Michael Myers--

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:30.508
bull****!!
(ax chopping)

00:00:30.508 --> 00:00:32.370
- While Carpenter and Hill
did date for a few years

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.120
in the late seventies while
they made "Halloween,"

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.410
the only child their
relationship birthed in real life

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.970
was one of the top 10 most lucrative

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.680
horror franchises of all time.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.430
The sixth entry of this
franchise would feature

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.448
many more connections to the 1978 original

00:00:43.448 --> 00:00:45.880
as well as many other surprising secrets.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.240
To learn the meaning behind
this pumpkin and more,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.383
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.800
(rock music)

00:00:56.211 --> 00:00:58.214
(train rumbling)

00:00:58.214 --> 00:01:00.290
Thank you for riding
the Halloween Express.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.560
The next stop is "Halloween:
The Curse of Michael Myers."

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.770
When we pull into the station,

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.660
you'll exit to the left on
the Producer's Cut platform.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.050
Yeah, I decided to use the
infamous producer's cut

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.230
as the basis for this episode
of "Things You Missed,"

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.900
but I will still mention one easter egg

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.200
that can only be found
in the theatrical cut.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.110
As with all the previous Halloween films

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.440
we've passed through on this journey,

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.492
I will once again be
joined by my co-conductor,

00:01:21.492 --> 00:01:23.110
Jimmy Champane.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:25.107
- So Zac I got these shirts
made from "Halloween 6"

00:01:25.107 --> 00:01:26.470
and we realized that it had

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:28.170
a not-friendly YouTube word on it,

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.400
so I spent all this time taping
it out and then I realized,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.060
this is my recording angle.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.970
It's a little known fact
that the producer's cut

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.730
of my last name has a G in it.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.550
- Yeah, I might need to take that joke out

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.290
of the CZ Cut of this video.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.040
I'll ask that everybody
please take their seats

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.370
and turn your attention to the windows

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.047
as we'll be running through
some more "Things You Missed."

00:01:46.047 --> 00:01:47.714
(blade whooshing)

00:01:47.714 --> 00:01:50.214
(eerie music)

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.740
As I mentioned, the parent
characters in "Halloween 6"

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.360
pay homage to the Carpenter-Hill duo,

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.360
who went on to collaborate
on many more films together

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.610
and one of which is the
1980 movie, "The Fog,"

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:02.123
which is also referenced
here in Curse, roll it.

00:02:03.247 --> 00:02:06.450
- [Tim] This is the famous
Tim Strode stomach pounder,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.620
you down for the challenge?

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:08.590
- If you've seen "The Fog,"

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.410
the line might sound very familiar.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:12.243
- Yes, ma'am.

00:02:12.243 --> 00:02:14.370
Mom, can I have a stomach
pounder and a Coke?

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.562
- In 1982, Carpenter and Hill
produced "Halloween III,"

00:02:16.562 --> 00:02:18.210
which is also honored here.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.460
The woman who runs the boarding house

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.550
next door to the Myers' house

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.240
goes by the name of Mrs. Blankenship,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.050
the same name as the
woman that Mr. Grimbridge

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.240
was supposed to have had dinner with

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.407
shortly before his disappearance
in "Season of the Witch."

00:02:28.407 --> 00:02:30.870
- "October 21st, dinner with Minnie."

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.647
Minnie Blankenship, he never showed up.

00:02:32.647 --> 00:02:34.010
- "The Curse of Michael Myers" begins

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:35.710
as we see an older Jamie Lloyd,

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.180
the little girl from
"Halloween 4" and "Halloween 5"

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.390
escaping from Smith's Grove Sanitarium.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.840
We don't know that it's Smith's Grove yet,

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.390
but if you pause the movie right here,

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.520
you can see that it's
actually a Smith's Grove van

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.882
chasing Jamie right before
it forces her off the road.

00:02:47.882 --> 00:02:50.012
But when we do officially
find out later on,

00:02:50.012 --> 00:02:53.090
it makes some nice parallels
to the previous movies.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.750
In "Halloween" and "Halloween 4,"

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.080
Michael Myers is the one
who escape Smith's Grove

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.070
on a rainy October 30th night.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:02:59.970
And now it's Jamie,

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.090
the girl once poised to be his successor.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.420
She even steals a car just as Michael did

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.050
after both of his escapes.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.500
There's also this very dark detail

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.220
in the producer's cut of "Halloween 6"

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.810
that implies that Michael Myers

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.210
is the father of Jamie Lloyd's child,

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.210
or as I learned to call him

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.770
in Cinemassacre's Monster
Madness, uncle dad.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:17.900
And you guys aren't going to believe this,

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.460
but it gets even darker from there.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.293
So in this movie,

00:03:20.293 --> 00:03:22.680
Jamie is played by an
actress named J.C. Brandy,

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.440
who was 20 years old at the time.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.960
But since Jamie was eight
years old in "Halloween 4,"

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.670
and this one takes place in 1995,

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.780
that would mean she's around 15 years old

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.680
when she delivers her baby and
that is just dark and gross.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.440
In the theatrical cut, they added the shot

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.900
of a bunch of embryos to imply

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.520
that Stephen is a test tube baby,

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.340
just to make it a little less disturbing

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.230
for the general movie going audience.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:47.410
But then in turn, they also
made it more disturbing

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.940
for religious movie goers.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.790
So yeah, it's like six in one
hand, half dozen in the other,

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.570
you're gonna offend someone
with a plot point like that.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.260
On a lighter note, there's
a weird coincidence

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.000
with this trilogy of "Halloween" movies

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.400
and the way that they're subtitled.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.297
So the first one is called

00:04:00.297 --> 00:04:02.370
"Halloween 4: The Return
of Michael Myers."

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.287
The fifth one is called

00:04:03.287 --> 00:04:05.650
"Halloween 5: The Revenge
of Michael Myers,"

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:06.877
and the sixth one is called

00:04:06.877 --> 00:04:08.950
"Halloween: The Curse of Michael Myers."

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.030
And weirdly enough, there's
another film franchise

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:12.340
that used the same subtitles

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.150
for it's fourth, sixth, and eighth movies,

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.200
and that franchise is "The Pink Panther."

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.907
Yes, Pink Panther four is called

00:04:17.907 --> 00:04:19.270
"The Return of the Pink Panther."

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.687
Pink Panther six is called

00:04:20.687 --> 00:04:22.110
"The Revenge of the Pink Panther,"

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.437
and Pink Panther eight is called

00:04:23.437 --> 00:04:25.160
"The Curse of the Pink Panther."

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.610
- Each of those Pink Panther movies

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.530
came out before it's
Halloween counterpart.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.940
And on top of that, there was
a Pink Panther remake in 2006,

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.273
one year before
Halloween's remake in 2007.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:37.960
And that remake had a sequel,
the "Pink Panther 2" in 2009,

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.217
just six months before the
Halloween remake sequel,

00:04:40.217 --> 00:04:41.230
"Halloween II."

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:42.867
But Pink Panther comparison aside,

00:04:42.867 --> 00:04:44.570
"The Curse of Michael
Myers" features Michael

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.440
coming back to Haddonfield
under the orders

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.030
of the mysterious Cult of Thorn

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.720
to steal Jamie Lloyd's baby
and sacrifice his half cousin

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.720
to pass his curse onto the child.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.080
With the franchise branching away

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.500
from the lore of the earlier movies,

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.160
this film tries to get back to basics

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.660
by tying the modern Michael Myers

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.120
back into the Celtic mythology

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.178
that backed "Halloween
II" and "Halloween III."

00:05:02.178 --> 00:05:04.710
Director Joe Chappelle even
brought back Donald Pleasence's

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.500
blatant mispronunciation of
the Gaelic festival Samhain

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.900
when Tommy Doyle explains
it all to Kara Strode.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.845
- According to Celtic legend,
one child from each tribe

00:05:14.845 --> 00:05:18.240
was chosen to be inflicted
with the Curse of Thorn,

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.606
so after the blood
sacrifices of its next of kin

00:05:20.606 --> 00:05:22.570
on the night of Samhain.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:23.520
- Halloween.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.410
- The sacrifice of one family

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.300
meant sparing the lives
of an entire tribe.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.880
- Samhain was explained in "Halloween II"

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.870
to be the source of
Michael's benevolent evil.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.460
And in "Halloween III," the motivation

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.910
for Conal Cochran's
terrifying Halloween plot.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.240
Curse takes the involvement to
the holiday one step further

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.900
by connecting it to these ancient runes

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.670
and explaining that the
dates of Michael's attacks

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:44.270
are determined by the appearance
of the Thorn constellation.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.440
And as Tommy explains this,

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.420
his face is way too close to Kara's hair.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:49.060
I guess he and Loomis have that in common.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.410
- [Loomis] Are you all right?

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.140
- Yeah, that definitely is a weird thing

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:53.130
that keeps happening.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:55.490
- Also every time I watch
this part about the runes now,

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:56.935
I'm just going to see the
word simp right there.

00:05:56.935 --> 00:05:58.340
Thanks internet.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.370
- A good amount of people

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.960
are just doing the reasonable
thing and just making jokes.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.360
- Anyway, at the end of Jamie's
escape from Smith's Grove,

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.310
she crashes into a
pumpkin patch at a barn,

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:08.480
a very similar location

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.700
to where she gave Michael
the slip in "Halloween 5."

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:13.413
Only this time, Jamie is not so lucky.

00:06:21.821 --> 00:06:24.321
(eerie music)

00:06:25.657 --> 00:06:28.027
Throughout this mini series
of Halloween franchise

00:06:28.027 --> 00:06:30.160
"Things You Missed" episode,
Jimmy and I have attempted

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.200
to point out all of the
lesser known callbacks,

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.050
the tributes, the homages
to the original Halloween.

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:36.760
Despite everything
we've already brought up

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:37.820
in the first five movies,

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.260
this sixth entry may be
the most derivative of all,

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.530
but there is another
massively iconic horror movie

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.920
that "The Curse of Michael
Myers" feels very influenced by,

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.317
and that is Stanley
Kubrick's 1980 masterpiece,

00:06:47.317 --> 00:06:48.350
"The Shining."

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.990
- It just so happens that your hosts today

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:52.310
are the perfect people to be
pointing out these connections

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.454
because I have a channel
that's practically dedicated

00:06:54.454 --> 00:06:57.499
to "Halloween" and Zac
never misses a reference

00:06:57.499 --> 00:06:58.850
to "The Shining."

00:06:58.850 --> 00:06:59.920
Zac wrote that joke to say

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:02.060
he never seems to miss a
reference to "The Shining,"

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.670
but I'm just going to
come out and tell you guys

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.840
he never misses one, it's a fact.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.956
- So if you're somehow
unfamiliar with "The Shining,"

00:07:07.956 --> 00:07:09.916
one, what are you doing with your life?

00:07:09.916 --> 00:07:11.970
And two, here's what you need to know.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:14.200
A former teacher named Jack
Torrance moves his family

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.830
into an isolated hotel for the winter

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.200
so he can take a job as the
hotel's winter caretaker.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.911
His son Danny has a psychic
and clairvoyant ability

00:07:19.911 --> 00:07:21.220
known as the shine,

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.580
allowing him to see the
ghosts of the hotel's past.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.760
After being shut in long enough,

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.740
the ghosts get to Jack,
causing him to go crazy

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:28.530
and to chase his family with an ax.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.960
- Halloween is an unlikely
franchise to do "The Shining"

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.930
because Michael Myers is a slasher villain

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.390
and "The Shining" is a
psychological horror movie.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.020
But if you keep any
franchise going long enough,

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.557
you're bound to try something new.

00:07:39.557 --> 00:07:41.050
- "The Shining" connection all starts

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:42.450
with Kara's son Danny.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.240
Not only does he share a
name with Danny Torrance

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:46.480
from "The Shining," but he's
a young boy with a bowl cut

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.040
and psychic voices in his head.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.830
Danny Strode hears the voice of Dr. Wynn,

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:51.800
who encourages him to
kill for Michael Myers.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.170
While Danny Torrance hears Tony,

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.630
his imaginary friend who warns him

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:56.610
about the dangerous posed by his shine.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:59.850
Danny Strode even has visions
just like Danny Torrance does.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.130
About halfway through the
movie, Dr. Loomis tries to warn

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:04.140
the Strodes that Michael Myers
is going to come for them.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:07.020
He does so by just straight
up walking into their house.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.080
- This dude is out of control,
he could have just waited

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.000
by the front door for them to come home.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.810
- After warning Debra about this danger,

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.010
she wants to get the
kids out of Haddonfield.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.890
- I'm getting the children out of here,

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:19.200
at least until I know what's going on.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.810
John, I want you to come with us.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:22.410
- This is basically beat for beat

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.280
the same conversation that Wendy Torrance

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.580
has with her husband in "The Shining"

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.180
when she tries to suggest that her Danny

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.997
should be driven to a doctor
in town for his wellbeing.

00:08:29.997 --> 00:08:34.067
- I think maybe he should
be taken to a doctor.

00:08:34.067 --> 00:08:38.104
- You think maybe he should
be taken to a doctor?

00:08:38.104 --> 00:08:38.950
- Yes!

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.090
- Earlier, I talked about
the character John Strode

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.550
being named after John Carpenter,

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:44.870
but perhaps there is a
second meaning here as well.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.380
He seems to represent Jack
Torrance in this story,

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.000
whose real name in "The
Shining" novel is John Torrance.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.908
I first realized the similarity
between these characters

00:08:51.908 --> 00:08:53.638
when I saw John Strode's first reaction

00:08:53.638 --> 00:08:55.520
to his wife's hysteria.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.050
- You've lost it, you know that, Debra?

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.350
You've just lost it.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.180
- It's very similar to Jack's
response to Wendy's claim

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.940
that someone is with them in the hotel.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.955
- Are you out of your (beep) mind?

00:09:04.955 --> 00:09:07.770
- They were both alcoholic,
abusive father figures.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.310
John Strode even drinks Jack
Daniels Tennessee Whiskey,

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:12.880
the very same beverage selected
by Jack in "The Shining."

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:15.780
Heck, they even use the
exact same line at one point.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.393
- Come out, come out wherever you are.

00:09:19.382 --> 00:09:22.200
- Come out, come out wherever you are.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.130
- The way Michael Myers approaches Debra

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.270
slowly as her back is
turned is very similar

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:28.210
to how Jack approaches
Wendy as she's reading

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.970
through the stacks of
paper on the typewriter.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.800
There's no sudden movement or jumps scare,

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.240
just the looming realization

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.830
that the character is not alone.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.940
Michael eventually takes
her out with an ax,

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.570
a weapon that he's never used before,

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:41.150
and at the time of making this
video has never used since.

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:42.180
Check me on that, Jimmy.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.170
- Yeah, that is the only time
Michael Myers uses an ax.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.680
- I'm sure it's no coincidence

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.440
that he wields Jack Torrance's
main weapon of choice.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.480
Both Dannys go into these hypnotic trances

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.260
later in the movie, and
both of their mothers

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:55.665
have a similar reaction at
the first sight of danger.

00:09:55.665 --> 00:09:57.114
- [Kara] Danny run!

00:09:57.114 --> 00:09:58.097
- [Wendy] Run and hide!

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.820
- Remember how I said
I'd be using one thing

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.630
from "Halloween 6's" theatrical cut?

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:03.960
Well, the room that Kara
escapes from in the sanitarium

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:07.010
is room 237, the same number
as the most haunted room

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:08.950
in the Overlook Hotel in "The Shining."

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:10.230
All right, I've had my fun,

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.680
I'm going to throw it
over to Jimmy Champane

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:14.460
to talk about all of the
"Halloween 1" connections.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.410
- Thanks Zac, I'll just start
at the beginning of the movie

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.530
and move on from there.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:18.940
When Jamie is escaping the asylum,

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:20.720
a woman who helps her out gets lifted up

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.230
and impaled on this thorn
like object on the wall,

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:25.640
which is very similar to how
Michael took out Bob Simms

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.161
back in '78, especially
how he just stands there

00:10:28.161 --> 00:10:29.650
and admires his work.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.380
- Also, Bob Simms has the
same last name as Barry Simms,

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:33.720
the radio show host in 6.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:35.360
Although I don't think they're related,

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.410
it doesn't seem like Barry
would be so exploitative

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.700
of Haddonfield and Michael
Myers if he had a family member

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.660
get whacked in the original rampage.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.270
- That night when Tommy Doyle logs on

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:44.900
to the project Michael Myers website,

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:46.930
Michael Myers face flashes on the screen

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.320
in the exact same way that
he appeared out of the dark

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:52.430
at the top of the Doyle's
staircase back in 1978.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:54.230
- If this came out today,
there would be a whole

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:55.990
project Michael Myers ARG

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.720
leading up to the release of the movie.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.830
- Yeah, I hope you're paying
attention, Night Mind.

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:01.950
Anyway, we're reintroduced
to Dr. Terence Wynn,

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.390
who appeared as a young
administrator at Smith's Grove

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.750
back in the first movie.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.810
- After 32 years, guess who
is finally relinquishing

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.840
his duties as Chief
Administrator of Smith's Grove?

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:13.050
- No, it's not the same actor,

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:14.839
but many people don't realize
that this is a character

00:11:14.839 --> 00:11:16.801
who was featured in the first movie.

00:11:16.801 --> 00:11:18.618
And it's definitely not their fault

00:11:18.618 --> 00:11:21.210
because he was only in like two shots.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:23.240
And of course, the other
"Halloween I" character

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.080
who came back in a big
way was Tommy Doyle.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.110
- He's always staring out his window.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:28.970
Last night I caught him watching me.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:30.600
- Tommy Doyle staring out a window?

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.510
I guess some things never change.

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:33.920
There's even a moment where young Danny

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.440
sees Michael Myers across
the way from Tommy's window,

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.690
just like young Tommy
did in the first movie.

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.330
Then there's the Haddonfield bus terminal

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:41.610
where we hear this announcement.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:45.880
- [Announcer] Bus 34 from
Peoria, Russellville and Gardner

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.540
with through service to Chicago, Illinois,

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.600
we'll be arriving in five minutes.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.450
- But Russellville is
one of the nearby towns

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.830
that was mentioned in
Halloween's I and II.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:56.580
- I remember over in Russellville.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:57.950
- We've still got a bunch more to cover

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.390
like "Halloween I" connections,

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:02.710
crew reference easter eggs
and this one single pumpkin,

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:04.220
but Zac is giving me the eye right now,

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:05.830
so I think we're supposed to take a break

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:08.639
and come right back with even
more "Things You Missed."

00:12:08.639 --> 00:12:11.556
(thunder crackles)

00:12:13.532 --> 00:12:16.032
(eerie music)

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:18.740
- In our previous episodes,

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:20.760
we talked about how Michael
always seems to appear

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.370
in tandem with these bedsheets,

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:24.290
which we theorized is
related to his tendency

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.290
to go after teenagers,
like his sister Judith,

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.150
who are always focused

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.760
on trying to go to bed with one another.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.410
At this point, I think the meaning is lost

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.260
and the bedsheets are just
more of a running gag.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:33.510
We see them hanging up outside

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:34.900
as Debra is chased out of the house

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.760
and Mr. Strode later
finds one of the sheets

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:38.450
covered in red in the washing machine.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.380
And this one isn't
technically a bed sheet,

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:42.460
but Michael notably
appears behind a curtain

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:44.900
as Mrs. Blankenship is
telling Michael's backstory.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:47.710
You can only spot him as the
lightning is striking outside.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:50.090
- Remember how in the original,
bullies harassed Tommy

00:12:50.090 --> 00:12:51.500
and make him fall on his pumpkin?

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.930
Well in Curse, something
very similar happens to Danny

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.270
who is startled and drops
his pumpkin on the ground,

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:59.220
only this time, Tommy's
the one who causes it.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:00.053
- Sorry.

00:13:00.053 --> 00:13:01.740
- At this point, Barry Simms is well into

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.110
his Halloween night radio
broadcast from Haddonfield

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.230
and during the commercial break,

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:07.190
Michael takes them out inside of a vehicle

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:09.500
in a very similar scene
to how we see Annie die

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:10.880
in the first "Halloween" movie.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:13.470
- Meanwhile, we check in on
Beth and her boyfriend Tim,

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:15.470
as she tells the story
of Michael's first attack

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:18.070
back in 1963 while
walking up the same stairs

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:19.960
that Judith Myers and
her boyfriend walked up

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:20.970
that very night.

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:23.090
Then they sleep together on the same bed,

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.570
or at least in the same bedroom

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.450
where Judith became Michael
Myers's first ever victim.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.730
After getting busy upstairs,

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:31.090
Tim jumps in the shower and
Michael hands him a towel

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:32.270
pretending to be Beth.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.660
This is something that seems
to happen once in each movie.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.690
Michael pretended to be
Bob under the ghost costume

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:38.160
to catch Linda off guard in 1.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.060
He pretended to be Bud

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.020
to get close to Karen
in the hot tub in II.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:43.730
He poses his Deputy Logan
to sneak up on Kelly in 4

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:46.030
and he takes the wheel
of Mikey's car in costume

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.760
to pick up Tina in 5.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.420
- And finally, when Kara
jumps out of a window

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:51.560
to escape Michael Myers
and the Cult of Thorn,

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.740
we see her lying face down on the ground

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:56.930
just like Michael did at
the end of "Halloween" 1978.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:59.062
- Now being the former
Illinois boy that I am,

00:13:59.062 --> 00:14:00.620
I've always been interested

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:02.570
in Haddonfield's location in the state.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.210
Haddonfield is not a real place,

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.590
but we've seen it placed
all over the Prairie State,

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:08.180
including south of Hardin County,

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.390
which is way at the bottom,

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.240
in Warren County, which
is way to the West,

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.160
and in Livingston County in the Northeast

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.320
closer to Lake Michigan.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.510
In "Halloween 6," we get more
of an exact map placement,

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:18.750
thanks to the bus map shown right here.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.610
The order of these
stops is pretty accurate

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:21.890
with the exception of Bloomington

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.540
and Funk's Grove being switched.

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:25.780
Using this map places
Haddonfield right around

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:27.820
where the village of
Odell is in real life,

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:29.330
which is part of Livingston County.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.489
I would say that this is a
nice attention to detail,

00:14:31.489 --> 00:14:33.740
but a newspaper later in
the movie still features

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:35.740
Haddonfield news in the
Warren County Gazette.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.820
As I've mentioned before,
Haddonfield is supposed to be

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.359
more of an Everytown, USA sort of place,

00:14:39.359 --> 00:14:41.900
so the actual location
isn't really that important,

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.980
but it can still be fun
to analyze this map.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.830
By the way, when we first
see the bus station,

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:48.380
there's a sign at the
desk that says back in 20.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.050
This is obviously a reference
to the franchise coming back

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.130
for "Halloween Kills,"

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:54.200
which was supposed to come out in 2020,

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.550
but it was delayed one year
due to the COVID-19 outbreak.

00:14:57.550 --> 00:14:59.110
- Shut up, Zac.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:14:59.943
- I'm guessing that joke

00:14:59.943 --> 00:15:01.880
will not be in the Jimmy Champane cut.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.130
- Speaking of locations though,

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.510
a whole bunch of the Thorn trilogy

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:06.320
was shot in Salt Lake City, Utah,

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:09.270
and we see a reference to this
in a magazine on John's desk

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:12.230
that's opened up to Salt Lake
City real estate listings.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.020
- There's also a one
crew reference easter egg

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:15.970
that I was able to spot in
the form of a sticky note

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.410
posted by the Strode's phone.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.390
It lists the number for Dr. Duane,

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.290
which is likely an odd to Duane Manwiller,

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.530
the first assistant
camera on "Halloween 6."

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.320
While we're talking about the
production side of things,

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.280
the film was distributed
by Dimension Films,

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.210
which is part of the
production company Miramax.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:31.454
Dimension was also responsible
for other high profile

00:15:31.454 --> 00:15:33.450
horror franchises, such as "Hellraiser,"

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.610
and it seems they really
wanted to push it at the time.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:37.120
According to "Rivers of Grue,"

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.180
one million dollars was
taken out of the budget

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.240
for "The Curse of Michael Myers"

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.830
and given to "Hellraiser: Bloodline,"

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.200
which would come out the next year.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.260
In addition to that,
"Halloween 6" director,

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.680
Joe Chappelle had to come and
finish directing "Bloodline"

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:50.060
uncredited after the
original director quit.

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:52.500
So it comes as no surprise
that they tried to promote

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:53.850
the new "Hellraiser" movie by putting

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.630
this pinhead inspired
jack-o-lantern on the front porch.

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:57.790
There are actually quite a few

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.440
additional horror movie references.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.370
Before Michael Myers is
first introduced in this one,

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:04.170
we see his shadow on a staircase,
just like the iconic scene

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:06.840
from the 1922 vampire flick "Nosferatu."

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:08.230
I think you probably already realized

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.110
Beth and Tim's costumes are supposed to be

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:12.320
Frankenstein's monster
and Bride of Frankenstein,

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.060
but I'm mentioning it here just in case.

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:15.990
Later on when Tommy takes Kara upstairs

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.960
to his boarding room, you'll
notice Mrs. Blankenship

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.350
watching Phantom of the Opera,

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.720
a movie with a very
famous unmasking scene,

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.105
perhaps a clue about Dr.
Loomis' unmasking of Dr. Wynn

00:16:24.105 --> 00:16:25.800
at the end of this cut.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.419
- [John Strode] Kids, my dear Debra,
are what's ruining this country.

00:16:28.419 --> 00:16:29.970
Everywhere you go, it's
the same damn thing.

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:31.973
It's no ******* respect.

00:16:32.833 --> 00:16:35.250
(soft claps)

00:16:38.019 --> 00:16:38.852
(crowd cheering)

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:41.340
- He's talking about millennials.

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.500
There are just a couple of
other miscellaneous items

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.510
that I want to point out.

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.240
When Barry is broadcasting his radio show

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:48.020
the day before Halloween, Jamie calls in

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.070
and claims that Michael
is back and he responds

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.150
by saying that it seems like
every loonie in the state

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.170
is calling tonight.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.030
What's the deal here?

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.630
Did radio shows not screen
their callers in the nineties?

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:59.050
In any event, I do love
the use of nineties slang

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.650
to foreshadow the
arrival of Michael Myers.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:02.960
- Tonight's going to be killer.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:05.230
- Finally, there's this shot
that I found kind of cool.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.980
When Kara gets back home
to the Myers' house,

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.520
you see the coat rack way in
the background, which is weird

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.580
because why would you
put a coat rack upstairs?

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:13.500
But it's dressed to almost
resemble the appearance

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:16.280
of Dr. Wynn with the trench
coat and the long brim hat.

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:17.410
It seems this was maybe supposed to be

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:19.340
a bit of a psychological
trick on the audience.

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:20.490
Like "The Shining" parallels,

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:22.760
another example of this Halloween
having a little bit more

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:25.480
of an affinity for psychological
horror than the others.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.120
Whether you prefer the producer's cut

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:28.910
where Loomis discovers
that Michael's escaped

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:30.960
and sees the thorn symbol
appear on his own arm,

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.460
or the theatrical cut where
Michael turns on the cult

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.730
and then gets drugged and
beat up by Tommy and Kara,

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:37.165
this is where we reach the end of the line

00:17:37.165 --> 00:17:39.260
on the Halloween express.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.140
For connections to the 20 year timeline,

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.680
including destinations
like "Halloween H2O"

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.450
and "Halloween Resurrection,"
go back to "Halloween II,"

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.610
where our linked terminal
will be opening in Fall 2022.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.620
In the meantime, make sure
you thank Jimmy Champane

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:52.920
for joining us on this entire journey

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:56.370
and sharing his expertise
on all things Halloween.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:57.670
- Also, if you haven't already,

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:59.200
please subscribe to Zac's channel.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.010
I know that he won't say it himself,

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:03.080
but there is a ton of work that goes into

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.650
each and every one of these videos

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.560
and he totally deserves your support.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.970
- So join us next year.

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:10.930
Yes, I said next year for new
"Things You Missed" episodes

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:13.080
on the rest of the Halloween franchise.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.590
Until then I've got a lot of
other horror topics to cover.

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:18.710
Make sure you subscribe CZsWorld
for new horrors every week.

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:20.830
Ring the death bell for all notifications.

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:23.000
And I will see you in the next one,

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.857
assuming we both survive.

00:18:25.857 --> 00:18:27.975
